On 2 December 2012 10:07, Michael Turniansky <<>mturn...@gmail.com> wrote:
Normally, you would use a connective, like "la djan .e la djim dunda lo dji=
ne la meris" (John and Jim gave a ring to Mary, which would mean they each =
gave her a ring) or "a djan jo'u la djim dunda lo djine la meris" (John alo=
ng with Jim gave a ring to Mary). In these cases, the x1 is the whole conne=
cted give "John and Jim", "John along with Jim")
--gejyspa
